### Lab 04: Registration, Login, and JWT
### Tested with VS Code REST Client

### 1. Register a new valid user
POST http://localhost:3000/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "israr_hussain",
  "name": "SYED ISRAR HUSSAIN",
  "password": "StrongPassword@2026"
}

### 2. Attempt duplicate registration (Expect 400: User already exists)
POST http://localhost:3000/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "israr_hussain",
  "name": "SYED ISRAR HUSSAIN",
  "password": "StrongPassword@2026"
}

### 3. Login with correct credentials (Expect 200: jwt_token)
POST http://localhost:3000/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "israr_hussain",
  "password": "StrongPassword@2026"
}

### 4. Login with invalid password (Expect 400: Invalid password)
POST http://localhost:3000/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "israr_hussain",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### 5. Login with non-existent user (Expect 400: Invalid user)
POST http://localhost:3000/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "unknown_user_999",
  "password": "SomePassword"
}
